#: src/important-programs.md:1
msgid "Important Programs"
msgstr ""

#: src/important-programs.md:3
msgid ""
"This page covers important programs and libraries supported by Redox as of "
"August 2026. <!-- don't forget to update this date -->"
msgstr ""

#: src/important-programs.md:5
msgid ""
"Redox is designed to be source-compatible with POSIX and Linux applications, "
"only requiring compilation or small patches."
msgstr ""

#: src/important-programs.md:7
msgid ""
"This page contains programs that are known to work well on Redox and "
"documents how well they were tested. All programs are compiled through our "
"package cross-compilation system called Cookbook, which includes the "
"configuration of all kinds of patches and forks that are required to make "
"them run on Redox."
msgstr ""

#: src/important-programs.md:9
msgid ""
"Everything on the following lists are tested on the x86_64 (Intel/AMD) CPU "
"architecture, other CPU architectures may not have been tested yet."
msgstr ""

#: src/important-programs.md:11
msgid ""
"(The broken or bad status may be outdated, consider to verify yourself to "
"confirm and possibly report regressions to us)"
msgstr ""

